<title canonical="true" type="psalm">A Psalm <i>or</i> Song for the sabbath day.</title><sup><b>1</b></sup> <i>It is a</i> good <i>thing</i> to give thanks unto the LORD, and to sing praises unto thy name, O most High:<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">A Psalm <i>or</i> Song for the sabbath day.</title><sup><b>2</b></sup> To shew forth thy lovingkindness in the morning, and thy faithfulness every night,<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">A Psalm <i>or</i> Song for the sabbath day.</title><sup><b>3</b></sup> Upon an instrument of ten strings, and upon the psaltery; upon the harp with a solemn sound.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">A Psalm <i>or</i> Song for the sabbath day.</title><sup><b>4</b></sup> For thou, LORD, hast made me glad through thy work: I will triumph in the works of thy hands.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">A Psalm <i>or</i> Song for the sabbath day.</title><sup><b>5</b></sup> O LORD, how great are thy works! <i>and</i> thy thoughts are very deep.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">A Psalm <i>or</i> Song for the sabbath day.</title><sup><b>6</b></sup> A brutish man knoweth not; neither doth a fool understand this.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">A Psalm <i>or</i> Song for the sabbath day.</title><sup><b>7</b></sup> When the wicked spring as the grass, and when all the workers of iniquity do flourish; <i>it is</i> that they shall be destroyed for ever:<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">A Psalm <i>or</i> Song for the sabbath day.</title><sup><b>8</b></sup> But thou, LORD, <i>art most</i> high for evermore.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">A Psalm <i>or</i> Song for the sabbath day.</title><sup><b>9</b></sup> For, lo, thine enemies, O LORD, for, lo, thine enemies shall perish; all the workers of iniquity shall be scattered.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">A Psalm <i>or</i> Song for the sabbath day.</title><sup><b>10</b></sup> But my horn shalt thou exalt like <i>the horn of</i> an unicorn: I shall be anointed with fresh oil.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">A Psalm <i>or</i> Song for the sabbath day.</title><sup><b>11</b></sup> Mine eye also shall see <i>my desire</i> on mine enemies, <i>and</i> mine ears shall hear <i>my desire</i> of the wicked that rise up against me.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">A Psalm <i>or</i> Song for the sabbath day.</title><sup><b>12</b></sup> The righteous shall flourish like the palm tree: he shall grow like a cedar in Lebanon.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">A Psalm <i>or</i> Song for the sabbath day.</title><sup><b>13</b></sup> Those that be planted in the house of the LORD shall flourish in the courts of our God.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">A Psalm <i>or</i> Song for the sabbath day.</title><sup><b>14</b></sup> They shall still bring forth fruit in old age; they shall be fat and flourishing;<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">A Psalm <i>or</i> Song for the sabbath day.</title><sup><b>15</b></sup> To shew that the LORD <i>is</i> upright: <i>he is</i> my rock, and <i>there is</i> no unrighteousness in him. <br />
